        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಏನೂ ಇಲ್ಲ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಏನೂ ಇಲ್ಲ (ēnū illa) — \"nothing\", literally \"anything, there isn't\". ಏನು (ēnu), \"what\", takes ‑ಊ to become \"anything\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಏನೂ ಇಲ್ಲ (ēnū illa) is native Dravidian: ēnū, \"even what\", from ēnu, \"what\" (DEDR 5151), and illa, \"is not\" (DEDR 2559). \"Not even anything\" is nothing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What, and not, make nothing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
