          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೌದಾ (haudā) is haudu, \"yes, it is so\", with -ā, the ending that makes a question. Haudu is usually explained as a form of āgu, \"to become\" (DEDR 333). DEDR 333 compares Sanskrit ām."
            }
          ]
        },
